<p local-id=3D"c17bd9e7bd66">single digit, indicates if claim is an institu=
tional claim or a professional claim</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"4ed22b2c-ecee-48e8-bbb7-cb1851fa674d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0b29f5337478">=E2=80=9CI=E2=80=9D - Institutional</p>
<p local-id=3D"7203494f01c8">=E2=80=9CP=E2=80=9D - Professional</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"1565cb2d-a1be-4fb9-b8b1-e9bc4ff854f7">
<td data-local-id=3D"3c3ae3b3-6b73-41a3-a117-479197b77356" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"81228867c697">Place of Service</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"4c8e0b5c-e2b4-4e7a-9a23-0024e7a967b5" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"03d11c896f38">CMS place of service code, where the care took=
 place</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"a994d37a-da22-48c5-8886-00459929f8bd" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9259b354a67c">11 - Office</p>
<p local-id=3D"1cf0d72bbf48">17 - Retail Health Clinic</p>
<p local-id=3D"70548191e512">20 - Urgent Care</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"17d0bc28-ca28-4cc5-82c4-f4e11e6f0ed7">
<td data-local-id=3D"d22ceb27-623b-4912-9249-32061dddd867" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"202255dddd49">Bill Type</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"2feeda89-b574-4ea2-8a19-e2cfe4d7be34" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9ad2631e2e85">Three digit code used on institutional claims.=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"416fbd2fc8ee">First Digit =3D Leading zero, ignored</p>
<p local-id=3D"b3003ef7d30b">Second Digit =3D Type of Facility</p>
<p local-id=3D"0c6d587d1a08">Third Digit =3D Type of Care</p>
<p local-id=3D"debcd7034087">Fourth Digit =3D Sequence of this bill in this=
 episode of care. Referred to as =E2=80=9Cfrequency=E2=80=9D code</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"320f3cf3-583d-4664-b7b9-5846a0e5623c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ddcc1a5e12be">131 - Hospital, Outpatient, Admit Through Disc=
harge</p>
<p local-id=3D"30e3560b0c80">111 - Hospital, Inpatient, Admit Through Disch=
arge</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"5be9918d-90ff-464d-b596-2e7e41181402">
<td data-local-id=3D"899b01c5-34d0-49ff-a4cc-b6efd655633c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"55b2b994ddbe">Rendering Provider Taxonomy</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"b810f2c1-513f-402a-be1f-aa12408e0ee9" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1f593b783927">What type of physician was seen</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"0077dbcc-a2d5-46a1-9a14-46ef2c7ea3e0" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"88be1242e194">&nbsp;</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"cbec8d1a-074b-453e-9769-b6b4f5d6a95b">
<td data-local-id=3D"5c396038-6c71-4f2e-9e79-5d5ca58a2953" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f4e622039ab9">CPT Code/CPT code specialty</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"dcc6bb92-6ee3-49af-b2de-9a1dd14b660b" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"99c864c9cb64">alpha numeric code indicating what types of se=
rvices were provided to the patient</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"ed886f0b-588d-45f9-941d-be3fde63d67c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d20d287a39d2">99211 Office Visit</p>
<p local-id=3D"7a0d876d4fca">97780 Acupuncture</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"7b956a55-5694-45f3-8b05-9c72956424cd">
<td data-local-id=3D"0b296715-1533-4066-bbc5-cc86a2809b5d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1b30b7334bc3">CPT Modifier Code</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"cecc7c06-6b83-4d30-a565-ead2ae9f06c0" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"df5798239dd2">Add additional modifier to the CPT code</p></t=
d>
<td data-local-id=3D"ed438f24-70b8-4b63-982c-6831cc4e87a5" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"8b276b6a0c7a"><strong>RT/LT:</strong> Right/Left side of the=
 body.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"b604cbd3-3679-4bcb-b5b1-3a32f088fc37">
<td data-local-id=3D"d2036daf-70aa-4daa-9169-38bd3ed462a9" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"78f321f1dd22">Diagnosis Code</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"82edc808-e1bb-45ba-8970-c5d0bc205264" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1a6f9b14ec77">What the patient being seen for</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"4ec0391e-48d8-4ef6-8a64-8360b5493ece" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"286dc64a02e3">&nbsp;</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"4b1c2c11-3a18-47ca-8612-ce3da8034466">
<td data-local-id=3D"976933a5-d57e-4084-b69b-5af5ac9899ee" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b507a3a5672a">DRG Code</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"58295f2d-4ff6-43bb-bd15-efdefead94a3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e3f100098376">Used for more complex episodes of care</p></td=
>
<td data-local-id=3D"5ea54ed3-9546-46a8-a7fd-2892e6cf1fe2" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"bb53d9c5cb08">&nbsp;</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"46691289-b40d-429f-908e-155acdaab44f">
<td data-local-id=3D"742e31b7-3050-4072-b910-8b2f03cf4cc3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"c300f13183b8">Revenue Code</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c4cbf542-5572-412b-a8c1-8d0bf1cc1dc4" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5184f8934730">Indicate what department of an institution/fac=
ility is billing the line item for</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"6f8b2218-d6cc-49aa-a88c-82fd23ed68ed" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f10d102fd350">&nbsp;</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"5843d85b577d"></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"b7de00ce567c" id=3D"Claims/GroupingRules-MatchedClaims=E2=
=86=92MatchedClaimsFinal"><strong>MatchedClaims =E2=86=92 MatchedClaimsFina=
l</strong></h2>
<p local-id=3D"2dbfbdc3ee16" style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><em>Procs Run: =
Common.MatchedClaimCompressor</em></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c196da2a5199">
<li local-id=3D"a518b1765b1c">
<p local-id=3D"74a6ac32eb06">Figure out final best rule for the claim and t=
he benefit code associated with it.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"0ce06b9ff031">
<li local-id=3D"98fd4ac80f42">
<p local-id=3D"b04525b1468f">Whatever rule is lowest =E2=80=9Crank=E2=80=9D=
 is chosen.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c348f2ed9885">
<li local-id=3D"d1acc6f3ac03">
<p local-id=3D"909163706ce9">Example: A facility claim may have multiple li=
ne items associated with various components related to a surgery.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"1a2ecf6dff6a">
<li local-id=3D"6a1f7a2f1f62">
<p local-id=3D"1fe40278b1d2">There may be several lines for the surgery ser=
vices themselves</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5dec520754b0">
<p local-id=3D"3ed150d8066a">There may be several for Labs, imaging, suppli=
es</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"6b9fa58f1c27" style=3D"margin-left: 60.0px;">Given the above=
, the surgery procedures would have an earlier rule rank than the labs/imag=
ing and would be the chosen benefit</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"2d49adc1a292">
<li local-id=3D"452b1f149391">
<p local-id=3D"f9422fc35cec">Exceptions:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"dea6b2a7d108">
<li local-id=3D"3c725f183926">
<p local-id=3D"86158f7da4a1">Any claim line with Allowed Amount of $0 gets =
its rule rank pushed to the end of the ranks. The reason being that we don=
=E2=80=99t want to give a benefit code for a service that is denied.</p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"3b25be76f172">
<p local-id=3D"2c4bd823625c">For partial preventive logic, preventive lines=
 are also put to the end of the rule ranks to allow non-preventive benefits=
 to be chosen.</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"496a319413bf" id=3D"Claims/GroupingRules-MatchedClaimsFinal=
=E2=86=92AdjudicatedClaims">MatchedClaimsFinal =E2=86=92 AdjudicatedClaims<=
/h2>
<p local-id=3D"81c0154c9e04" style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;">Procs Run: Simp=
lePay.AccumulatorAdjudicator</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"bbb242bfcec4">
<li local-id=3D"c1660f8f3bb9">
<p local-id=3D"5c9fdf9cd7ab">Final patient/member responsibility is calcula=
ted based on multiple criteria</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"f7b92d62cf30">
<li local-id=3D"0e3852e3ec70">
<p local-id=3D"567ce1802639">If Copay &lt; TotalAllowedAmount, take TotalAl=
lowedAmount</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e8a2c1a99723">
<p local-id=3D"c0e4930267ad">If the member is at their Out of Pocket Max (O=
OPM), then put memberResponsibilityAmt to $0</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0671118a263d">
<p local-id=3D"bf114616dec4">If the Copay/TotalAllowedAmount causes the mem=
ber to hit their OOPM, set MemberResponsibilityAmt tot he difference (EX: M=
ember has a copay for $500, but they are only $250 from hitting their OOPM,=
 in this case, MemberResponsibilityAmt is set to $250 up to OOPM)</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"1ab3931eecd9"></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"593669ad1c99" id=3D"Claims/GroupingRules-NewRuleEngineThrou=
ghNected">New Rule Engine Through Nected</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"0ecf331a8042" id=3D"Claims/GroupingRules-Possiblesolutions"=
>Possible solutions</h3>
<p local-id=3D"90ddb5b36497">Break claims processing into smaller batch pro=
cesses through decision trees</p>
<p local-id=3D"17157303613f" style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;">Example: Claims=
 already come into two types =E2=80=9CInstitutional=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9CP=
rofessional=E2=80=9D. This could split the claims processing into smaller w=
orkflows for each claim type and break up the monolithic current process wh=
ere every rule is ran to find matches for claims</p>
<p local-id=3D"9396f0004fea" style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;">Possible furthe=
r filtering:</p>
<p local-id=3D"5c7cbccade8b" style=3D"margin-left: 60.0px;">For Institution=
al, bill type codes mainly drive whether a claim is Inpatient vs Outpatient=
.<br></p>
<p local-id=3D"0fe44dabebd9">The rules naturally cluster into a handful of =
major domains:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"166692e9-cb18-47a0-8bb9-59f=
47b5a04fc" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"4897376c-562c-4c49-9360-2f743119632a">
<th data-local-id=3D"0c7d7697-a2a2-43f3-ba63-f372021bb54c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"82e45d7d4e5e">Domain</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"f3add470-1b73-4f86-8360-ec56e99ebe64" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"fb89f86c1b90">Typical Attributes</p></th>
</tr>
